  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Raytheon contracted with the federal government for $8.2B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Raytheon won 370 awards so far this fiscal year. Raytheon has an average award size of $22.2M. Raytheon obligations are down 23.6% year over year. Raytheon obligations by fiscal year show a trajectory of $5.9B in FY21, $7.4B in FY22, $7.6B in FY23, $7.8B in FY24, $10.7B in FY25, and $8.2B in FY26. Raytheon revenue is concentrated in a few NAICS markets: Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounts for $6.3B of FY2026 to date obligations, and Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing accounts for $959M. Raytheon also has material obligations in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $567M and in Engineering Services at $147M. This mix shows heavy exposure to missile and space manufacturing plus durable follow-on work in R&D and engineering services.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Raytheon federal obligations by market?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest market, accounting for $6.3B of FY2026 to date obligations. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing is the next-largest market at $959M. Raytheon also has notable obligations in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $567M and in Engineering Services at $147M. The remaining top markets range from $123M down to $2.8M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has Raytheon’s federal obligations trended recently?",
        "body": "Raytheon obligations rose from $5.9B in FY21 to $10.7B in FY25, then fell to $8.2B in FY26 to date. Raytheon obligations are down 23.6% year over year. Raytheon won 370 awards in FY2026 to date with an average award size of $22.2M. This mix reflects larger and fewer awards in the current fiscal year compared with prior years."
      }
    ]
